        "id": "EX-GRAM-G-hsk1-numbers-r5-02-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "Hundreds and thousands",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "Place 百 and 千 after their leading digit. Insert 零 for an internal missing place; do not read ordinary amounts as disconnected digit strings.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "一百零一。",
                "pinyin": "yī bǎi líng yī 。",
                "meaning": "One hundred and one.",
                "audio": "97e53061891e3c573e9b9103137363512cd92ccfe405e89dd1f66e880cedc6e9"
              },
              {
                "text": "一千零五。",
                "pinyin": "yī qiān líng wǔ 。",
                "meaning": "One thousand and five.",
                "audio": "50cfddde70de118630d9df40ae4c4a73566ffbfd6801c108fc4aa14ee6365f10"
              },
              {
                "text": "九千九百九十九。",
                "pinyin": "jiǔ qiān jiǔ bǎi jiǔ shí jiǔ 。",
                "meaning": "Nine thousand nine hundred and ninety-nine.",
